cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Settlemint: a self-settling event market for NEAR"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sarkar"
    given-names: "Dipankar"
repository-code: "https://github.com/doom2quake/settlemint-near"
abstract: >-
  A NEAR-native event market that settles itself. A resolver opens a binary
  Yes/No market with a named function-call access key; stakers commit
  yoctoNEAR while it is open; when the outcome is known the resolver records it
  once and an operator pays every winner pro rata in a single resumable pass.
  The last winning claimant sweeps the rounding dust so escrow lands at exactly
  zero and no stake is stranded, and a permissionless void escape hatch lets
  every staker withdraw their own stake if the resolver never resolves. This
  milestone-1 release is the NEAR Rust settlement core plus a Python mirror kept
  in cross-language parity by tests. Testnet only, no mainnet.
keywords:
  - near-protocol
  - self-settling-market
  - pari-mutuel
  - autonomous-agent
  - rust
  - smart-contract
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
